    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "O’Farrell Property is delighted to present this opportunity to acquire a one-off detached two-storey new-build home in the sought-after countryside location of Shanragh.\r\n\r\nExtending to an impressive c. 264m², the property is offered to the market with a builders finish, providing the successful purchaser with the opportunity to complete and personalise the home to their own taste and specification.\r\n\r\nThe well-proportioned accommodation comprises an entrance hallway, living room, spacious kitchen/dining room, utility room, guest WC and a versatile second reception room, which could be utilised as a home office, additional living space or fifth bedroom. Upstairs, there are four bedrooms, with the generous primary bedroom benefiting from a walk-in wardrobe and en-suite, together with a main family bathroom.\r\n\r\nThe property occupies a superb c. 0.79-acre site, offering generous gardens and ample outdoor space. A substantial detached garage of c. 45m² is also included, providing excellent additional storage or workshop space and benefiting from both a roller door and separate pedestrian access.\r\n\r\nThe property is equipped with an air-to-water heat pump, private well, septic tank, mechanical ventilation with heat recovery and electricity. The home boasts an attractive natural stone façade complemented by granite window cills, double-glazed windows and an impressive A BER rating.\r\n\r\nAlso included in the sale is an allowance towards the installation of a fitted kitchen, further enhancing the opportunity for the new owner to create a home tailored to their individual requirements.\r\n\r\nThe property enjoys a peaceful rural setting in Shanragh while remaining within easy reach of a range of local amenities and larger surrounding towns. The location offers an excellent balance between countryside living and everyday convenience, with nearby villages providing access to local shops, schools, sporting facilities, pubs and other essential amenities. The larger towns of Athy and Carlow are all readily accessible, providing a wider selection of supermarkets, schools, restaurants, retail outlets, healthcare facilities and leisure amenities. The property also benefits from convenient access to the regional road network, making it an ideal location for those commuting to Carlow, Kildare, Laois and further afield. \r\n\r\nThis is a rare opportunity to acquire a substantial, energy-efficient new-build property on a generous site, while having the freedom to finish and style the interior to your own specification."
      },
